 Use structured text (ST code) to design a function block (FB) for a PLC program that involves two nested loops.
The outer loop (i) iterates from 0 to 10, and the inner loop (j) iterates from 10 to 100 with a step size of 2.
During each iteration, if the flag is TRUE, the loop exits, and the count is updated
to keep track of how many times the inner loop executed.
Ensure that the count does not exceed the expected maximum of iterations
and that loop variables stay within their defined bounds.

FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_NestedLoopControl
VAR
i : INT;
j : INT;
flag : BOOL;
count : INT := 0;
some_var : INT;
END_VAR

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
